<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Telebras results denied-paper.</title>
<headline>Brazil Telebras results denied-paper.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's federal telecoms company Telebras has sent a letter to stock exchanges, distancing itself from the firm's 1996 annual results as announced by the Telecommunication Ministry, a newspaper said.</p>
<p>Telebras said Wednesday's announcement of a 3.2 billion reais ($3.08 billion) profit in 1996 by Telecommunications Minister Sergio Motta could merely have been an estimate, Gazeta Mercantil said.</p>
<p>In a statement sent to Brazilian and U.S. stock exchanges, Telebras said its 1996 accounts had not been closed yet and no date had been set for the publication of the 1996 results, Gazeta said.</p>
<p>((--Simona de Logu, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 507 4151))</p>
